Alembic migrations for Business Execution Ledger.

Full policy: ../docs/PERSISTENCE-MIGRATION-POLICY.md. Summary below.

TWO DIRECTORIES, ONE ACTIVE CHAIN
==================================

migrations/postgresql_versions/
    The ACTIVE chain (alembic.ini's version_locations points here only).
    PostgreSQL-only — every revision's upgrade()/downgrade() refuses to
    run against any other dialect. Started at the PostgreSQL Migration
    Epoch (see the policy doc for the commit SHA).

migrations/versions/
    INERT. The pre-Phase-2D.1-P SQLite-era chain, frozen byte-for-byte
    at the LEGACY MIGRATION FREEZE ANCHOR (commit
    b94f572528e25a620bf1a78bd2e26d12547b0212). Never wired into Alembic
    tooling again — kept only as historical reference. Do not add new
    files here, and do not point any config at it.

HARD RULE — MIGRATIONS ARE IMMUTABLE
=====================================

Once a file under either directory above is committed, it must never be
modified, deleted, or renamed. A schema correction is always a NEW
forward migration. Enforced mechanically by
../tools/check_migration_immutability.py (pre-commit locally, full
branch-history mode in CI) — see the policy doc for the exact rules
(M1-M10).

RUNNING MIGRATIONS
===================

    export BEL_DATABASE_URL=postgresql+psycopg://user:password@host:5432/bel
    alembic upgrade head
    alembic current
    alembic check

SQLite is a test-only convenience with no active chain here — build its
schema via Base.metadata.create_all() (see tests/conftest.py), not
alembic.
